     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Mccall-May Medical Group\nPatient: Patrick Gomez DOB: 06/30/1963 Sex: M MRN: 281028\n\nEncounters:\n 2024-12-25 back strain BP 145/89 Wt 197\n 2024-04-07 Cancer (see type table) BP 146/87 Wt 184\n 2023-07-20 URI BP 148/80 Wt 197\n 2022-10-31 Cancer (see type table) BP 148/88 Wt 181\n 2022-02-11 Cancer (see type table) BP 138/86 Wt 185\n 2021-05-24 flu shot BP 143/85 Wt 188\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Melanoma cancer, stage I (s/p treatment ~10.8 years ago) - controlled; medications: none\n\nPatient History:\nPatrick Gomez, a 61-year-old male, has a significant medical history notable for stage I melanoma diagnosed in June 2013. The melanoma was treated approximately 10.8 years ago, and the patient remains in a controlled state with no current medications required for the cancer.\n\nSocial Gomez is a former smoker, having smoked cigarettes at a rate of 10 per day starting in March 1995 and quitting in January 2021. He reports consuming alcohol at a rate of approximately one drink per week. \n\nFamily History:\nThe patient's mother had breast cancer, which was diagnosed when she was 46 years old, and she passed away at the age of 52. His father had a stroke, with the age of onset not specified, and he passed away at the age of 55. Additionally, the patient's mother is currently alive and has type 2 diabetes, which was diagnosed when she was 66 years old.\n\nRecent Encounters:\n- On December 25, 2024, Mr. Gomez visited for a back strain. His blood pressure at that time was 145/89 mmHg, and his weight was 197 pounds. \n- April 7, 2024, Mr. Gomez had a follow-up appointment regarding his cancer. His blood pressure was 146/87 mmHg, and his weight was 184 pounds.\n- On July 20, 2023, he visited for an upper respiratory infection (URI). His blood pressure was 148/80 mmHg, and his weight was 197 pounds.\n- On October 31, 2022, another follow-up for his cancer was conducted. His blood pressure was 148/88 mmHg, and his weight was 181 pounds.\n- On February 11, 2022, another cancer was documented. His blood pressure was 138/86 mmHg, and his weight was 185 pounds.\n- On May 24, 2021, Mr. Gomez visited for a flu shot. His blood pressure was 143/85 mmHg, and his weight was 188 pounds.\n\nPhysical Exam Findings (Recent Visits):\n- Vital signs were stable within normal limits across all visits.\n- HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. Eyes: No scleral icterus. Ears: No abnormalities. Nose: No nasal discharge. Throat: No erythema or exudates.\n- Neck: No lymphadenopathy. Carotids: No bruits.\n- Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm. No"
